{number: 30}
{title: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Hark! The herald [G] angels [C] sing,
"Glory to the [F] new-born [G] King!
[C] Peace on earth, and [G] mercy [Am] mild,
[D7] God and sinners [G] reconciled!"
[C] Joyful, all ye [F] nations [G] rise,
[C] Join the triumph [F] of the [G] skies;
[F] With the angelic [Dm] host pro-[A7] claim,
"[Dm] Christ is [G7] born in [C] Bethlehem!"
[F] Hark! the herald [Dm] angels [A7] sing,
"[Dm] Glory [G7] to the [C] new-born King!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Christ, by highest [G] heav'n a-[C] dored,
Christ, the ever-[F] lasting [G] Lord,
[C] Late in time be-[G] hold Him [Am] come,
[D7] Offspring of a [G] virgin's womb.
[C] Veiled in flesh the [F] Godhead [G] see,
[C] Hail the incarnate [F] Dei-[G] ty!
[F] Pleased as Man with [Dm] man to [A7] dwell;
[Dm] Jesus, [G7] our Im-[C] manuel!
[F] Hark! the herald [Dm] angels [A7] sing,
"[Dm] Glory [G7] to the [C] new-born King!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Hail, the heav'nly [G] Prince of [C] Peace!
Hail, the Sun of [F] Righteous-[G] ness!
[C] Light and life to [G] all He [Am] brings,
[D7] Ris'n with healing [G] in His wings.
[C] Mild, He leaves His [F] throne on [G] high,
[C] Born that man no [F] more may [G] die;
[F] Born to raise the [Dm] sons of [A7] earth;
[Dm] Born to [G7] give them [C] second birth,
[F] Hark! the herald [Dm] angels [A7] sing,
"[Dm] Glory [G7] to the [C] new-born King!"
{end_of_verse}
